Given \(f(x)=3-2 x\), determine the equation of \(f^{-1}(x)\).

\section*{Solution}

Let \(y=f(x)\)
\[
y=3-2 x
\]
To determine the inverse of \(f(x)\), switch \(x\) and \(y\).
\[
\begin{aligned}
x & =3-2 y \\
2 y & =3-x \\
y & =\frac{3-x}{2} \\
f^{-1}(x) & =\frac{3-x}{2}
\end{aligned}
\]
