The point, \(P(\theta)=\left(-\frac{1}{6}, y\right)\), lies on the unit circle and is located in Quadrant III. Determine the exact value of \(\csc \theta\).

\section*{Solution}
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/cb04cf73-5c15-41ee-bfc2-b302a5cbcd7a-41.jpg?height=404&width=402&top_left_y=724&top_left_x=243)
\[
\begin{aligned}
(-1)^{2}+y^{2} & =(6)^{2} & & 1 / 2 \text { mark for substitution } \\
1+y^{2} & =36 & & \\
y^{2} & =35 & & 1 / 2 \text { mark for solving for } y \\
y & = \pm \sqrt{35} & & 1 \text { mark for consistent value of } \csc \theta \\
\csc \theta & =-\frac{6}{\sqrt{35}} & & (1 / 2 \text { mark for quadrant; } 1 / 2 \text { mark for value) } \\
& \text { or } & & \\
\csc \theta & =-\frac{6 \sqrt{35}}{35} & &
\end{aligned}
\]

Notes:
Accept any of the following values for \(y: y= \pm \sqrt{35}, y=\sqrt{35}\), or \(y=-\sqrt{35}\).